 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "zevachim.97a.6",
   "daf": "97a",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "וַחֲכָמִים אוֹמְרִים: עַד זְמַן אֲכִילָה כּוּ׳. מַאי קָאָמַר? אָמַר רַב נַחְמָן אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר אֲבוּהּ: מַמְתִּין לָהּ עַד זְמַן אֲכִילָה, וַהֲדַר עָבֵיד לַהּ מְרִיקָה וּשְׁטִיפָה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «And the Rabbis say:» One may not continue using it in this manner; rather, one must perform scouring and rinsing «before» the end of the «period» during which «partaking» of the particular cooked offering is permitted. «What» is the mishna «saying? Rav Naḥman said» that «Rabba bar Avuh said: One waits for» the copper vessel «so long as» it remains «the period of partaking, and then» he «performs scouring and rinsing on it.»"
  }
 ],
